message: "If you use this software or its recorded results, please cite it as below."
title: "UOR-R4 Geometric Language Model"
type: software
version: "pre-alpha"
date-released: 2026-10-09
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/UOR-Foundation/uor-r4"
url: "https://uor-foundation.github.io/uor-r4/"
authors:
  - family-names: Allard
    given-names: Casey
  - name: "UOR Foundation"
keywords:
  - language model
  - geometric deep learning
  - quaternion
  - multiplier-free inference
  - exact addressed memory
  - Rust
abstract: >-
  UOR-R4 is an experimental autoregressive language model written in Rust that
  asks whether geometry (R4/S3/H4 quaternion state and transport, prime
  addressing, exact Z[phi] arithmetic and fixed zeta-zero phases) can replace a
  transformer's run-time machinery. Training is offline Rust; serving uses
  integer and table lookups with no floating point and no multiplier
  instruction. The project is pre-alpha: no model holds a useful conversation
  yet, and the repository records both positive and negative measured results.
